 "seesTitle": "What Santuari de Cura sees",
 "seesHTML": "From the 542 m summit terrace the whole south-west of the island lies below you, and the eclipse plays out over the Tramuntana skyline 40 km away: totality happens directly above the S'Esclop silhouette (+0.43\u00b0 despite its 926 m), with \u22481.9\u00b0 \u2014 3\u00bd sun-widths \u2014 of clear sky in between. You also get what no beach offers: the Moon's shadow visibly racing up the Bay of Palma toward you. The trade: the crescent doesn't reach the sea \u2014 it sets into the S'Esclop\u2013Plan\u00edcia saddle at ~20:46.",
 "capHTML": "Horizon panorama from Santuari de Cura: terrain silhouettes with projected angular altitudes against the sun's descent. The crescent is last visible at \u224820:46.",
 "recoTitle": "Around Santuari de Cura",
 "recoHTML": "<li><b>The west terrace of the monastery</b> \u2014 summit car park, 30 min from Es Trenc; arrive well before 19:30 to hold a west-facing spot.</li><li><b>Randa road miradors</b> \u2014 the pull-offs below the summit share the geometry.</li><li><b>Monti-sion (Porreres)</b> \u2014 the neighbouring hilltop is <em>risky</em> (0.6\u00b0); don't substitute it.</li>",
 "verdictText": "Totality with 1.8\u00b0 to spare \u2014 terrain takes the crescent at \u224820:46"
